{"surah": 107, "verses": [{"ayah": 1, "text": "أَرَءَيْتَ ٱلَّذِى يُكَذِّبُ بِٱلدِّينِ ", "translation": "Have you seen the one who denies the Recompense?", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "أَرَءَيْتَ", "translit": "َtْyَءَrَaʾ", "root": "راي"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يُكَذِّبُ", "translit": "ُbِّhdَkُy", "root": "كذب"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "بِٱلدِّينِ", "translit": "ِnyِّdlٱِb", "root": "دين"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 2, "text": "فَذَٰلِكَ ٱلَّذِى يَدُعُّ ٱلْيَتِيمَ ", "translation": "For that is the one who drives away the orphan", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَذَٰلِكَ", "translit": "َkِlَٰhdَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِى", "translit": "àِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يَدُعُّ", "translit": "ُّʿعُdَy", "root": "دعع"}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "ٱلْيَتِيمَ", "translit": "َmyِtَyْlٱ", "root": "يتم"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 3, "text": "وَلَا يَحُضُّ عَلَىٰ طَعَامِ ٱلْمِسْكِينِ ", "translation": "And does not encourage the feeding of the poor.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَلَا", "translit": "āَlَw", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "يَحُضُّ", "translit": "ُّḍُḥَy", "root": "حضض"}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَلَىٰ", "translit": "ٰàَlَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "طَعَامِ", "translit": "ِmāَʿعَṭ", "root": "طعم"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "ٱلْمِسْكِينِ", "translit": "ِnyِkْsِmْlٱ", "root": "سكن"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 4, "text": "فَوَيْلٌ لِّلْمُصَلِّينَ ", "translation": "So woe to those who pray", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "فَوَيْلٌ", "translit": "ٌlْyَwَf", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "لِّلْمُصَلِّينَ", "translit": "َnyِّlَṣُmْlِّl", "root": "صلو"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 5, "text": "ٱلَّذِينَ هُمْ عَن صَلَاتِهِمْ سَاهُونَ ", "translation": "[But] who are heedless of their prayer[1] -", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هُمْ", "translit": "ْmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "عَن", "translit": "nَʿع", "root": ""}, {"id": 4, "arabic": "صَلَاتِهِمْ", "translit": "ْmِhِtāَlَṣ", "root": "صلو"}, {"id": 5, "arabic": "سَاهُونَ", "translit": "َnwُhāَs", "root": "سهو"}], "hasIhya": true}, {"ayah": 6, "text": "ٱلَّذِينَ هُمْ يُرَآءُونَ ", "translation": "Those who make show [of their deeds]", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "ٱلَّذِينَ", "translit": "َnyِhdَّlٱ", "root": ""}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "هُمْ", "translit": "ْmُh", "root": ""}, {"id": 3, "arabic": "يُرَآءُونَ", "translit": "َnwُءٓāَrُy", "root": "راي"}], "hasIhya": false}, {"ayah": 7, "text": "وَيَمْنَعُونَ ٱلْمَاعُونَ ", "translation": "And withhold [simple] assistance.", "words": [{"id": 1, "arabic": "وَيَمْنَعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعَnْmَyَw", "root": "منع"}, {"id": 2, "arabic": "ٱلْمَاعُونَ", "translit": "َnwُʿعāَmْlٱ", "root": "عون"}], "hasIhya": false}], "tafsir": {"4": [{"arabic": "أما الآيات فقوله تعالى فويل للمصلين الذين هم عن صلاتهم ساهون الذين هم يراءون وقوله عز وجل والذين يمكرون السيئات لهم عذاب شديد ومكر أولئك هو يبور قال مجاهد هم أهل الرياء وقال تعالى إنما نطعمكم لوجه الله لا نريد منكم جزاء ولا شكورا فمدح المخلصين ينفي كل إرادة سوى وجه الله والرياء ضده وقال تعالى فمن كان يرجو لقاء ربه فليعمل عملا صالحا ولا يشرك بعبادة ربه أحدا // حديث نزول قوله تعالى فمن كان يرجو لقاء ربه الآية فيمن يطلب الآخرة بعباداته وأعماله أخرجه الحاكم من حديث طاوس قال رجل إني أقف الموقف أبتغي وجه الله وأحب أن يرى", "english": "As for the verses: it is His saying, Exalted is He: {فويل للمصلين الذين هم عن صلاتهم ساهون الذين هم يراءون} — \"So woe to those who pray, those who are heedless of their prayer, those who make a show\" {Al-Ma'un 107:4-6}. And His saying, Mighty and Majestic is He: {والذين يمكرون السيئات لهم عذاب شديد ومكر أولئك هو يبور} — \"And those who scheme evil deeds — for them is a severe punishment, and the scheming of those — it shall perish\" {Fatir 35:10}. Mujāhid said: \"They are the people of riyā'.\"", "book_title": "Condemnation of Status and Ostentation", "section_title_ar": "Section 810", "section_title_en": "The Second Half of the Book on Seeking Status and Rank through Acts of Worship — Being on Riya' (Ostentation/Show), Its Blameworthiness, and Its Treatment", "section_index": 810, "anchors": "- Root: راءى (rā'ā)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root is الرؤية (vision/sight); المراءاة is showing oneself to another, derived from mutual seeing (تفاعل) — the act of displaying one's deeds for another's observation.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): الرياء is the seeking of rank (الجاه) and station (المنزلة) in the hearts of men through displaying acts of obedience — it is the antithesis of الإخلاص (sincerity), which restricts intention solely to the Divine Face (وجه الله).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (Haqiqah): mutual visual perception. Metaphorical (Majaz): the spiritual \"seeing\" of one's deeds by creatures, seeking their approbation — a transfer from physical sight to the heart's craving for social esteem.\n- Root: سها (sahā)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Neglect, heedlessness, inattention; the one who is \"sāhin\" is oblivious to the essence and time of an act.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): السهو is the heart's vacancy from awareness of the true import of an affair; in the verse {الذين هم عن صلاتهم ساهون} it denotes neglect of the prayer's time and conditions, coupled with ostentation in performing it.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: distraction. Metaphorical: the soul's diversion from the Hereafter toward the gaze of creatures.\n- Root: مكر (makara)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Crafty scheming, deception; the \"makr\" of the ostentatious is their covert corruption of good deeds.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): المكر is the turning of another from his intent by subtle concealment; the \"sayyi'āt\" (evil deeds) of the riyā' practitioners are their acts of worship corrupted by show — their scheming \"yabūr\" (perishes) because it is built on other than God.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: stratagem. Metaphorical: the hypocritical display of piety as a ruse to capture hearts — a \"makr\" that boomerangs to perdition.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — In {إنما نطعمكم لوجه الله}, the particle إنما confines the motive exclusively to God's Face, negating all secondary aims (جزاء or شكورا); this is the grammatical seal of ikhlāṣ against riyā'.", "content_type": "hadith", "topic": "Prophetic traditions and scholastic commentary by Al-Ghazali, from 'Condemnation of Status and Ostentation'", "badge": "Hadith"}], "5": [{"arabic": "الذين هم عن صلاتهم ساهون قال هو الذي يسهو في صلاته فلا يدري على كم ينصرف أعلى شفع أم على وتر وقال الحسن هو الذي يسهو عن وقت الصلاة حتى تخرج وقال بعضهم هو الذي إن صلاها في أول الوقت لم يفرح وإن أخرها عن الوقت لم يحزن فلا يرى تعجيلها خيرا ولا تأخيرا إثما واعلم أن الصلاة قد يحسب بعضها ويكتب بعضها دون بعض كما دلت الأخبار عليه وإن كان الفقيه يقول إن الصلاة في الصحة لا تتجزأ ولكن ذلك له معنى آخر ذكرناه وهذا المعنى دلت عليه الأحاديث إذ ورد جبر نقصان الفرائض بالنوافل (2) وفي ال", "english": "One person departed from this world [without ever having been present in prayer], and another was asked: \"Do you find yourself thinking of anything of this world during the prayer?\" He said: \"No — neither in the prayer nor outside of it.\"", "book_title": "Mysteries of Prayer", "section_title_ar": "Section 142", "section_title_en": "The Revival of the Religious Sciences — Book of Prayer, Section 142: On the States of the Humble (al-Khāshiʿīn) and the Lightening of Prayer", "section_index": 142, "anchors": "- Root: صلا (ṣ-l-w)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core root denotes the kindling of fire and burning; secondarily, the act of prayer (ṣalāh) as devotional worship.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): The root's primary sense is \"ignition by fire\" (īqād bil-nār); its application to prayer is a transferred usage denoting the \"burning\" of the soul in devotion and the purification of the heart from heedlessness.\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal (ḥaqīqah) sense is physical burning; metaphorical (majāz) sense is the spiritual \"burning\" of the heart in humble devotion before God.\n- Root: خشع (kh-sh-ʿ)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is lowliness, submissiveness, and being humbled; applied to the earth as \"low-lying\" ground.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"Al-Khushūʿ is supplication/abasing oneself (al-ḍarāʿah), and it is most frequently used for what appears upon the bodily members, whereas al-ḍarāʿah is most frequently used for what is found in the heart. Therefore it was said: 'When the heart is humble (ḍaraʿa), the bodily members become submissive (khashaʿat).'\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: to be low and submissive. Metaphorical: \"an earth that is khāshiʿah\" (low-lying, untilled), \"voices hushed (khashaʿat al-aṣwāt)\" — indicating the outward manifestation of inward humility.\n- Root: سها (s-h-w)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is heedlessness, forgetfulness, and inattention.\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): Forgetfulness (al-sahw) is the heart's neglect of what it is obligated to attend to; it is the opposite of presence of mind (ḥuḍūr).\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: to be heedless of something. Metaphorical: the heart's \"absence\" from what the tongue and body are engaged in.\n- Root: وري (w-r-y)\n  * Lisan / Ayn: Core meaning is to conceal, to cover; also, to strike fire from a flint (warā al-zand).\n  * Al-Raghib (Mufradat): \"It is said: wāraytu kadhā — I concealed it. And the Prophet (peace be upon him) 'when he intended a raid, he would dissemble with something else (warā bi-ghayrihī)' — that is, he would conceal one matter and manifest another.\"\n  * Al-Zamakhshari (Asas): Literal: to cover/conceal. Metaphorical: \"your fire-sticks have struck fire (warat zanādī)\" — meaning your affair has become manifest and your condition evident.\n- Sibawayh Rule: باب الحصر والتقييد بإنما (Restriction & Focused Predication) — The particle innamā restricts the predicate to the subject alone, negating it for all else. This is critical for understanding the ḥadīth: \"إنما يكتب للعبد من صلاته ما عقل منها\" (Only that part of his prayer which he comprehended is written for the servant) — the restriction here is not on the act of prayer itself but on what is \"written\" (rewarded) of it, which is exclusively that portion attended to with understanding.", "content_type": "dua", "topic": "Al-Ghazali on supplications, prayers, and their spiritual power, from 'Mysteries of Prayer'", "badge": "Du'a"}]}, "wordTiming": {"minshawi": {"1": [[1, 350, 1473], [2, 1473, 2436], [3, 2436, 3705], [4, 3705, 5210]], "107:1": [[1, 350, 1473], [2, 1473, 2436], [3, 2436, 3705], [4, 3705, 5210]], "2": [[1, 210, 1182], [2, 1182, 2119], [3, 2119, 3210], [4, 3210, 4800]], "107:2": [[1, 210, 1182], [2, 1182, 2119], [3, 2119, 3210], [4, 3210, 4800]], "3": [[1, 170, 1210], [2, 1210, 2180], [3, 2180, 3055], [4, 3055, 4112], [5, 4112, 5450]], "107:3": [[1, 170, 1210], [2, 1210, 2180], [3, 2180, 3055], [4, 3055, 4112], [5, 4112, 5450]], "4": [[1, 170, 1422], [2, 1422, 3540]], "107:4": [[1, 170, 1422], [2, 1422, 3540]], "5": [[1, 260, 1775], [2, 1775, 2211], [3, 2211, 2728], [4, 2728, 4530], [5, 4530, 6390]], "107:5": [[1, 260, 1775], [2, 1775, 2211], [3, 2211, 2728], [4, 2728, 4530], [5, 4530, 6390]], "6": [[1, 260, 1632], [2, 1632, 2027], [3, 2027, 5290]], "107:6": [[1, 260, 1632], [2, 1632, 2027], [3, 2027, 5290]], "7": [[1, 80, 2024], [2, 2024, 3670]], "107:7": [[1, 80, 2024], [2, 2024, 3670]]}, "abdulbasit": {"1": [[1, 650, 1510], [2, 1520, 2370], [3, 2380, 3420], [4, 3430, 4030]], "107:1": [[1, 650, 1510], [2, 1520, 2370], [3, 2380, 3420], [4, 3430, 4030]], "2": [[1, 600, 1500], [2, 1510, 2380], [3, 2390, 3220], [4, 3230, 4490]], "107:2": [[1, 600, 1500], [2, 1510, 2380], [3, 2390, 3220], [4, 3230, 4490]], "3": [[1, 550, 970], [2, 980, 1820], [3, 1830, 2480], [4, 2490, 3510], [5, 3520, 4910]], "107:3": [[1, 550, 970], [2, 980, 1820], [3, 1830, 2480], [4, 2490, 3510], [5, 3520, 4910]], "4": [[1, 850, 1980], [2, 1990, 3680]], "107:4": [[1, 850, 1980], [2, 1990, 3680]], "5": [[1, 600, 1680], [2, 1690, 2110], [3, 2120, 3300], [4, 3310, 4740], [5, 4750, 6190]], "107:5": [[1, 600, 1680], [2, 1690, 2110], [3, 2120, 3300], [4, 3310, 4740], [5, 4750, 6190]], "6": [[1, 600, 1700], [2, 1710, 2170], [3, 2180, 4950]], "107:6": [[1, 600, 1700], [2, 1710, 2170], [3, 2180, 4950]], "7": [[1, 400, 1770], [2, 1780, 3070]], "107:7": [[1, 400, 1770], [2, 1780, 3070]]}, "abdulbasit_mujawwad": {"1": [[1, 2400, 4610], [2, 4620, 6060], [3, 6070, 12230], [4, 12240, 13860]], "107:1": [[1, 2400, 4610], [2, 4620, 6060], [3, 6070, 12230], [4, 12240, 13860]], "2": [[1, 3000, 4680], [2, 4690, 5900], [3, 5910, 7460], [4, 7470, 8670]], "107:2": [[1, 3000, 4680], [2, 4690, 5900], [3, 5910, 7460], [4, 7470, 8670]], "3": [[1, 3450, 4530], [2, 4540, 5940], [3, 5950, 7370], [4, 7380, 9830], [5, 9840, 10890]], "107:3": [[1, 3450, 4530], [2, 4540, 5940], [3, 5950, 7370], [4, 7380, 9830], [5, 9840, 10890]], "4": [[1, 1200, 4762], [2, 4762, 12042]], "107:4": [[1, 1200, 4762], [2, 4762, 12042]], "5": [[1, 3010, 4780], [2, 4790, 5430], [3, 5440, 6690], [4, 6700, 9260], [5, 9270, 15100]], "107:5": [[1, 3010, 4780], [2, 4790, 5430], [3, 5440, 6690], [4, 6700, 9260], [5, 9270, 15100]], "6": [[1, 3120, 5870], [2, 5880, 9810], [3, 9820, 11790]], "107:6": [[1, 3120, 5870], [2, 5880, 9810], [3, 9820, 11790]], "7": [[1, 950, 4270], [2, 4280, 8750]], "107:7": [[1, 950, 4270], [2, 4280, 8750]]}, "abdulbasit_warsh": {"1": [[1, 450, 2763], [2, 2763, 4533], [3, 4533, 6232], [4, 6232, 8942]], "107:1": [[1, 450, 2763], [2, 2763, 4533], [3, 4533, 6232], [4, 6232, 8942]], "2": [[1, 450, 1537], [2, 1537, 2836], [3, 2836, 3843], [4, 3843, 5964]], "107:2": [[1, 450, 1537], [2, 1537, 2836], [3, 2836, 3843], [4, 3843, 5964]], "3": [[1, 450, 1517], [2, 1517, 2536], [3, 2536, 3457], [4, 3457, 4767], [5, 4767, 6852]], "107:3": [[1, 450, 1517], [2, 1517, 2536], [3, 2536, 3457], [4, 3457, 4767], [5, 4767, 6852]], "4": [[1, 450, 2584], [2, 2584, 5337]], "107:4": [[1, 450,